A||||7||JohnnyK||Carbon deposits on inside of tailpipe||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-15-2000||04:13 PM||||Well, I guess this means something is going amiss in the engine (it's an 85 SE 4cyl). I get fairly bad mileage, and it blows out a bit of black smoke. Also, I can sometimes smell raw fuel. I replaced the o2 sensor, with no results, so what could be wrong. I have not replaced the rotor (and the car has been sitting a few years) or done timing. What else could be the cause? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-15-2000||05:16 PM||||A bad MAP sensor can cause symptoms like yours.  (So can forgetting to hook up your MAP sensor after installing a new intake manifold gasket.)||||reg||1
